        "title": "One of the sacred temples for Lord Shiva devotees",
        "text": "This in one of the 8 UNESCO heritage sites in Nepal. This temple is dedicated Lord Pasupathi or 'lord of the animals', who is an incarnation of Lord Shiva. Lord Shiva is considered the national deity in Nepal.  This is the largest temple complex.\n\nI particularly enjoyed the Bagmati aarti in the late evening. It is truly mesmerizing. It is performed by 3 priests simultaneously and some devotees dance the 'thandava', a cosmic dance by Lord Shiva.\n\nStrange to see the aarati being performed on one side of the river bank whilst a dead body awaits cremation right opposite it.\n\n",
