        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r640029632-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "God of the gods",
        "text": "I visited the Hindu Shiva shrine, also recognized by most Hindus as the head of most Shiva temples, on two occasions: To seek blessings of the lord, and to observe crematory function of a relative. On both occasions my mind was fortunately stable and there was nothing but curiosity. Pashupatinath temple is a beautiful pagoda style architecture, and in the inside the ''Linga\" at its top has four faces, of which one face has \"Ardha Nareswar\" depicting Shiva and Parbati conjoined--and emitting a message that both are one. Since it has a notice stating that the temple is for Hindus only, for others they can go around its back following the \"Bagmati\" river and can witness cremation at the \"Ghats\" as well as the temple architecture from outside. Byapta",
        "review_tip": null,
