      {
        "review_id": 639404413,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r639404413-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Be prepared",
        "text": "As someone who grew up in a culture where we are pretty much shielded from the reality of death, this temple was quite the humbling experience.  I didn’t understand why they don’t allow foreigners or even foreign Hindus in the Temple.  That was the only negative against the place.  Walking around the grounds was great and then we stumbled upon an area where funerals/cremations were taking place.  Me and my mate had a good 5 minute debate about what we were looking at.  When they went to re-kindle one of the fires and we saw the human skull, the debate was settled.  There was something very weird but also very spiritual/enlightening about this area of the temple.  I wasn’t prepared for what was going on, and it left me a bit shell shocked, mostly because they allowed pretty much anyone to view these ceremonies, take pictures, and tour around.  I definitely recommend going, but do be mindful that people are mourning their loved ones.",
