      {
        "review_id": 639308716,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r639308716-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "A very educational religious site",
        "text": "We took a taxi from Boudanath Stupa to visit Pashupatinath temple for about 250npr. We were immediately approached by a man who was very polite and assisted us in paying for the entrance fee for 10USD per pax. \n\nInitially we thought it would be another scam (it could have been) , but turns out that he was offering his guide services around at around 20USD for about an hour and a half around the site. \n\nAt first we declined his services, but as we walked to the entrance of the temple, we realised that he offered information that was interesting and would make the expensive visit make more sense. We learnt that foreigners were not allowed into the main temple. Only \"true blue\" hindus could enter and offer their prayers. But we we go around the area and take pictures at a respectful distance. The non-temple area was quite a large area to cover. \n\nWe also witnessed several cremation ceremonies going on in the Pashupatinath temple, along the river bank. We were enlightened by the guide on the procedures. The procession was a sight to behold. \n\nThere were also religious men who lived in caves, whom offered tourists or devotees photogtraohy moments at a fee. There were also \"religious\" men who were offering palm reading services along side the river bank. \n\nApparently, a short segment of the Dr Strange movie was also filmed there. So that was interesting. \n\nAll in all, we did not regret paying for the guide and was intrigue by this attraction.\n",
        "review_tip": null,
